  "observations": [
    "The actual original was a flat cyan slab over a nearly black band. Round05 has clear native stone courses, readable broad face turns, purposeful lower shoulder facets and a blue grounded body. It visibly advances toward the fixed softly lit blue stone target.",
    "The current finish was judged independently of mesh identity. Distinct angular face patches and gentle bevel transitions explain the upper stones and lower shoulders at128; at phone32 their grouping and course separation survive. The diffuse frontal pooling seen in04 no longer obscures those face turns.",
    "E/W were checked especially closely against the04 blocker. The lower exposed cap now reads as blue planes with a restrained localized course-edge accent, rather than the prior conspicuous cyan light pools. That accent remains visible at32 but functions as an edge/course cue, with no luminous spot, white glare, alpha spill or loss of cap volume. This is a judgment of this exact current visible treatment, not a waiver for arbitrary bands or seams.",
    "The coherent course treatment achieved in04 is preserved. Crown/collar shading integrates with neighboring stones, and the native/independent three-module N/S runs do not return to bright post-and-panel framing.",
    "All18 exact declared hero/preview paths were directly inspected. Complete lossless strips cover all4 desktop screenshots at actual128 resolution; every phone/backend case was directly inspected at32. Own all4 saved-source native replays, all4 native joins, matched03/04/05 full-frame comparison and fresh independent phone captures were also inspected.",
    "Native and independent joins are visually clean at their actual ports in all4. No old interior groove or current interior facet edge is misidentified as a connector failure. Current low-amplitude RGB/exterior partial-alpha differences are retained numerically and separately assessed in the actual visible images.",
    "The active native normalized-normal analytic illumination and new matched collar field are valid within the original method freedom. Their graph type is not the basis of approval. Actual consumed normal/albedo/radiance roles were resolved from active current links and independently evaluated, including the current SINE/COSINE operations."
  ],
